    #When K in KNN is too large, the algorithm starts considering many neighbors — 
    # even those far away or belonging to other classes — which dilutes the influence of the most relevant points.
    #Underfitting occurs: It fails to capture the true structure of the data because distant, irrelevant neighbors dominate.
    #Bias increases, variance decreases: Predictions become more stable but less accurate.
