    #MSE (Mean Squared Error): Measures average squared difference between predicted and actual values — lower is better.
    #R² (Coefficient of Determination): Measures how much variance in the target is explained by the model — closer to 1 is better.
    #--------------------------------------------------------------------
    #9. Why R² cannot be greater than 1?  
    #Because it represents the proportion of variance explained; 1 means perfect prediction, 
    # and values above 1 are mathematically impossible.
